# Only the package and its documented drivers belong in this repo. Everything
# below is run output, a scratch driver, or a working copy that accumulates in
# the working tree and has twice been swept into a commit by a careless
# `git add -A`.
#
# A .gitignore does NOT affect files that are already tracked, so nothing
# currently in the repo is removed by this. To commit something that matches a
# rule below, use `git add -f <path>`.

# Shell drivers. These are per-machine: they hardcode absolute paths and name
# specific datasets, so they are not reusable and do not belong in the package.
# createfiles.sh is the exception -- it is Stage 0 in the documentation.
*.sh
!scripts/createfiles.sh

# Run logs and captured stdout
*.log
*.out

# Timestamped and reason-tagged working copies: foo.R.bak_cores, but also
# foo.R.bak9_1104 -- the numbered form does not match bak_*, so both patterns
# are needed.
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.bak[0-9]*
*.orig
*.rej
*.stale_*

# R build and check artefacts
*.Rcheck/
..Rcheck/
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
*.tar.gz

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Manuscripts and figures. Deliberate figures go in with `git add -f`.
*.docx
*.pdf
*.png

# GrASE_simulation is a SEPARATE repository, symlinked in here for convenience.
# It must never be committed as part of this one.
GrASE_simulation

# Editor and tooling state
.claude/
.DS_Store
*.swp
